To upload a release asset with OctoKit SDK v3, call the `uploadReleaseAsset()` helper on an `OctoClient` instance, providing the required fields:

```js
await client.uploadReleaseAsset({
  owner: "octo",               // repository owner (required)
  repo: "hello-world",         // repository name (required)
  release_id: 1,               // ID of the target release (required)
  asset_name: "bundle.tar.gz", // name for the uploaded asset (required)
  body: fs.createReadStream("bundle.tar.gz") // file data as Buffer/Stream (required)
  // optional: content_type (defaults to application/octet-stream)
});
```

`uploadReleaseAsset()` sends the binary file to the specified release [uploads-reference:uploadreleaseasset:1]. The uploads helpers, including this method, are documented under the Uploads reference for SDK v3 [uploads-reference:uploads-reference-sdk-v3:0].
